{"timestamp": 1779393716.917269, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I found Alice\u2019s body in Weapons. My route was Electrical \u2192 Cafeteria \u2192 Weapons. When I entered Weapons, Charlie was there standing right by the body, and I reported immediately.\n\nEarlier I had seen Alice and Diana together in Upper Engine around ticks 11\u201313, but that was before the last meeting. This round after the meeting, I only saw Charlie in Weapons with Alice dead. I\u2019m not hard-locking without hearing Charlie and Diana, but Charlie definitely needs to explain why they were on the body."}}
{"timestamp": 1779393732.425529, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve, I literally just walked into Weapons from Cafeteria! I stepped into the room, saw the body, and before I could even hit the report button, you reported it. If I had killed Alice, why on earth would I just stand right on top of the body waiting for someone to walk in? I would have left immediately. \n\nHonestly, it feels like you killed her, waited for someone to walk in, and then instantly self-reported to frame them since we're down to the final 3. Diana, we really need to hear where you were this round. If you weren't anywhere near Weapons, then Eve has to be the Duck trying to pull a fast one to win the game. Don't fall for this, Diana. I'm voting Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779393754.4159691, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 28, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I was not near Weapons this round. After the meeting/respawn I went lower engine \u2192 storage and was in Storage when the report happened. I didn\u2019t see either of you this round, so I can\u2019t personally vouch for anyone\u2019s exact timing.\n\nFor older info: before the last meeting I saw Eve in Upper Engine around ticks 11\u201313, Frank around Electrical/Medbay, and Alice in Weapons around ticks 20\u201322, but that was before the previous meeting so it doesn\u2019t prove this kill.\n\nRight now it\u2019s basically Eve\u2019s report versus Charlie\u2019s \u201cI just walked in.\u201d Since Alice\u2019s body was in Weapons and Eve says Charlie was standing right on it, that\u2019s the only concrete accusation we have. Charlie\u2019s defense is possible, but in final 3 a self-report frame is also possible. I have to choose based on likelihood, and being found on the body is worse than reporting it. I\u2019m leaning Charlie."}}
